                <mxCell id="91" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;idea of CGI&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;The idea of CGI is that a user logs in to the web server using a username and password. The CGI program validates the credentials and generates the appropriate HTTP response for each possible outcome (successful login, invalid credentials, errors, etc.). Another role of CGI is to execute external programs or scripts, such as Python or shell scripts, and return their output as the HTTP response.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" parent="255" vertex="1">
